["amend","bug-1794190919",1794770922,"b3ac7798-996d-442d-8cb4-812824948701",{"acceptance":["FetchBranchToRef and RestoreEvidence hold the common-git-dir staging.lock flock across clone-local fetch, and BeginPerRunRef, beginArmatureTmpNS, and sweep deletes of refs/armature-tmp and _armature-run refs take the same flock, so a peer release cannot drop those refs mid-negotiation.","BeginPerRunRef allocation stays outside the staging flock, so linked worktrees may still hold overlapping live nonces.","FIFO-gated interleaving (mkfifo, not sleep) covers the #435 fetch-versus-release race in TestStagingLock_SerializesFetchAgainstPeerRelease_REQ_435 and TestRestoreEvidence_StagingLockBlocksPeerReleaseMidFetch_REQ_435, and TestOpsBackup_ParallelMovingTip_NoSharedTrackingLock_REQ_TOPTIER_S12_T1 keeps t.Parallel.","make check exits 0"],"definition_of_done":"Peer release cannot delete clone-local refs/armature-tmp or _armature-run refs during another worker's ops-backup fetch: fetch and staging-ref delete share a common-git-dir staging flock, while BeginPerRunRef allocation stays unlocked (GitHub #435 / PR #464). FIFO interleaving tests cover that race and ParallelMovingTip stays t.Parallel. make check is green at the delivery head."},1]
